  "m1_notes": [
    "Derived from official ZGWS source: https://github.com/zsibot/MATRiX_Python_SDK/blob/7c63590c21beba2f633c344b96bc29a695d7a807/model/zgws/zgws.xml",
    "Native MJCF retains source masses, inertial quaternions, joint ranges, motors, sensors, contact geometry, and floating base.",
    "Contact geoms use display group 3; non-contact visual geoms retain their existing group. Collision masks are unchanged.",
    "URDF omits the root body's scene placement and freejoint; downstream scene placement remains separate.",
    "URDF expresses each source principal-axis inertia as the equivalent full tensor R diag(I) R^T in the link frame, with inertial RPY zero; masses, centers of mass, and physical inertias are preserved.",
    "The four URDF wheel joints retain the source finite +/-99999 rad ranges; this is not a claim of validated wheel control.",
    "URDF velocity=1.0 rad/s is a description/planning placeholder because the source specifies no physical velocity limits.",
    "actuatorfrcrange values are source model settings, not verified continuous hardware torque specifications.",
    "The upstream home keyframe is commented out. Its qpos is exposed only as an assembly/FK candidate; its ctrl is ignored.",
    "Use transformed wheel collision mesh vertices or the compiled model to set contact height; bbox centers alone are only geometric references.",
    "Binary STL headers beginning with 'solid' are normalized only when their byte layout confirms binary STL; triangle data is unchanged."
  ],
  "piper_notes": [
    "Official Piper H with-gripper Xacro expanded once; standalone gripper not appended.",
    "Removed the source world/world_to_base_link; caller mounts piper_base_link with a fixed transform.",
    "Visuals use verbatim official collision STL, with flat gray material. DAE scenes/materials were NOT converted.",
    "Official STL coordinates/scales retained; no guessed millimeter conversion applied.",
    "Mesh collision uses MuJoCo convex hulls, so concavities and fine contact geometry are simplified.",
    "Contact friction/condim and equality solver settings use explicit MuJoCo default assumptions; source URDF has no calibrated contact data.",
    "Official link mass, COM and inertia retained; visual/collision geoms contribute zero inferred mass.",
    "URDF keeps official width master and mimic; MJCF removes empty master and constrains finger2=-finger1.",
    "One gripper motor acts on finger1 in N; opening width=2*q_finger1. This is not a calibrated grip-force interface.",
    "Seven motor force bounds are URDF effort limits, not independently verified hardware ratings; velocity limits need controller enforcement.",
    "TCP at gripper_base+[0,0,0.138] m is nominal; camera, hand-eye calibration and accessory payload are outside this module.",
    "No freejoint, hardware interface, auto-enable, controller gain, or successful dynamics claim is supplied.",
    "URDF mesh paths assume description; MJCF mesh paths assume project root. Rebase when writing elsewhere.",
    "Explicit base_link/link1 adjacent collision exclusion also applies when the Piper root is welded to world; source overlapping STL shells are unchanged."
  ],
